  "body": "### Summary\nAs a maintainer, I want `ReaderSettingsWatch` to stop reading settings once it is stopped, so that a reader that left the screen never applies a late change and the test stops flaking.\n\n### Report\n`ReaderSettingsWatchTests.aStartedWatchReadsNowThenFollowsEveryChangeUntilStopped` failed once on an iPad simulator under heavy load (PR #834 round 2, mac/M1, 2026-11-11). It passed 2/2 when rerun alone. The assertion after `stop()` failed: the watch read a settings change after it was stopped. `ReaderSettingsWatch` came with #786 (#750).\n\n### Hypothesis to check, not assume\n`stop()` cancels the task, but a change notification already delivered, or a hop to the main actor already queued, still runs the read. The fix is to check cancellation (or a stopped flag) before applying, and to cover the class: every `ReaderSettingsWatch` path.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] The race is reproduced deterministically: an injected notification arrives between `stop()` and the read. The test fails at `dev-swift`.\n- [ ] No read after `stop()` on any path; the test passes 50 times in a row under a parallel full-suite run.\n\nRelated: #564 (another flaky app test).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
